      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. This order is double the maximum. It would put the patient at serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum, and may be what was meant.\n- **1700 mg total daily, split into doses.** For example, 850 mg twice daily.\n- A different dose or frequency altogether.\n\nPlease tell me the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily really is intended, please confirm that explicitly. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy or the prescriber first."
      }
